This product includes design patterns and small components adapted from the
following MIT-licensed projects. Their copyright notices are retained here as
required by the MIT License:

- screen-use (https://github.com/tongriyaotxt/screen-use), MIT License.
  Adapted: UI Automation element enumeration + ValuePattern read/write ideas,
  screen-change fingerprinting and stuck-classification, verify-by-observation.

- clacky (https://github.com/Raynan00/clacky), MIT License, which itself vendors
  the "Bitshank/clicky-windows" companion shell (MIT).
  Adapted: offline wake-word + energy-VAD ambient-listening approach, and the
  action risk-classification tiers.

Design patterns studied for independent reimplementation (NO source copied):
- shorka (https://github.com/lllichtmaher/shorka) — barge-in, spoken confirmation,
  tool-call repair, focus-centric UIA reading. No license was published; only the
  observable design was used, reimplemented from scratch.
- VisionAssistantPro (https://github.com/mahmoodhozhabri/VisionAssistantPro),
  GPL-2.0 — accessibility/NVDA-coexistence lessons only; NO code reused or linked.
